a\n\n- Given the current state of kserve/kserve#5839, when the diff is analyzed against the\n  RHOAI-consumed v1alpha2 surfaces, then a written findings document enumerates every\n  downstream adaptation required beyond the authentication context, or explicitly concludes\n  none are needed.\n- Given the OpenShift deployment context, when RBAC and TLS surfaces are reviewed, then any\n  required adjustments (roles, bindings, CA/TLS configuration for KEDA Prometheus triggers)\n  are identified and described precisely enough to scope the downstream work.\n- Given the upstream merge state and review trajectory, when the carry/wait assessment is\n  performed, then a recommendation with rationale is produced covering: wait for upstream\n  merge vs. carry the patch downstream, and the trigger conditions that would flip the\n  recommendation.\n- The findings are reviewed with the strategy's pending architecture review in mind and any\n  conflicts are escalated as open items rather than silently resolved.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- De-risks HLR-1 (P0: standalone KEDA with user-defined triggers without WVA) — this\n  investigation does not directly implement the requirement; it resolves the unknowns that\n  gate both downstream implementation work streams covering HLR-1.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36951,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5a4845098be9430","agent_id":"a4eeb449d7b52be09","session_id":"c67b7b09-8e50-4c38-b7b7-230c45313c19","uuid":"372262d5-3c60-4e3d-b216-dee0714c9915","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:24:14.341Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8008"}
