c fields\n49\t  (`pollingInterval`, `cooldownPeriod`, `triggers`) and examples for Resource, External,\n50\t  and PodMetric trigger types.\n51\t- Scale-to-zero and scale-from-zero guidance: how `idleReplicaCount: 0` releases GPU\n52\t  capacity, and recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control\n53\t  queue metrics, including example ScaledObject templates (mitigating the\n54\t  misconfigured-trigger reliability risk).\n55\t- Realistic cold-start expectations for scale-from-zero latency, referencing the fast\n56\t  model startup RFEs (RHAIRFE-7753, RHAIRFE-7599, RHAIRFE-7139) and headroom\n57\t  configuration recommendations for latency-sensitive workloads, aligned to the agreed\n58\t  p50/p95 scale-from-zero targets.\n59\t- KEDA as a documented prerequisite: RHOAI does not auto-install KEDA (overlay 0008);\n60\t  installation guidance referencing the GitOps repository (ODH-ADR-0007).\n61\t- Instructions for operators to reference the TriggerAuthentication resource in KEDA\n62\t  trigger definitions for authenticated Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift.\n63\t- Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments (e.g., polling-interval\n64\t  impact at 2000-GPU fleet scale), incorporating the Performance/PSAP team's answer.\n65\t- Troubleshooting paths and a supported configuration matrix (paths x topologies x\n66\t  trigger types).\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- The decision guide covers all three allocation modes (WVA-mediated, standalone KEDA,\n71\t  static) with use-case-based recommendations, reviewed for technical accuracy against\n72\t  the implemented API surface.\n73\t- Configuration recipes exist for each supported workload shape and trigger type, and\n74\t  every example is technically reviewed against the implementation (validated against the\n75\t  architecture context files: workload-variant-autoscaler.md, kserve.md, llm-d.md,\n76\t  odh-model-controller.md, and overlay 0011).\n77\t- Scale-from-zero documentation includes recommended trigger configurations using EPP\n78\t  queue metrics with example templates, and documents realistic cold-start time\n79\t  expectations aligned to the agreed p50/p95 scale-from-zero targets.\n80\t- KEDA installation is documented as a prerequisite with guidance referencing the GitOps\n81\t  repository, consistent with platform policy (no auto-installation).\n82\t- Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments is included, reflecting the\n83\t  Performance/PSAP input.\n84\t- Troubleshooting guidance covers common failure modes: misconfigured triggers failing\n85\t  the zero-to-one transition, metric outages, and CEL validation errors for invalid\n86\t  path combinations.\n87\t- All content passes the Red Hat docs content process including technical review by the\n88\t  engineering teams that implemented the autoscaling paths.\n89\t\n90\t## HLR Traceability\n91\t\n92\t- HLR-7 (P1): well-lit path documentation covering both autoscaling paths with decision\n93\t  guide, configuration recipes per workload shape, and troubleshooting.\n94\t- Supports HLR-4 (P0): documented recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations\n95\t  (the mechanism itself is implemented in the controller work stream).\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b86ae54f4cb05af3","agent_id":"ada836977a2e1d943","session_id":"c67b7b09-8e50-4c38-b7b7-230c45313c19","uuid":"52d3ac78-c60a-48a8-b8ac-b3688d86af08","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:40:01.541Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-863bd63e675f2607","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
