{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a497dee97a469bfb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n3\ttitle: Standalone KEDA autoscaling path for LLMInferenceService in the KServe llmisvc-controller\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: Serving Orchestration\n6\tteam: Serving team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8008-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream adaptation investigation finds kserve/kserve#5839\n15\t    requires downstream adaptation beyond the authentication context (RBAC/TLS adjustments)\n16\t    or recommends carrying the patch downstream, rewrite this epic's scope to include\n17\t    those adjustments and the patch carry with backport; the core API/validation/controller\n18\t    design from kserve/kserve#5646 is unchanged.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Standalone KEDA autoscaling path for LLMInferenceService in the KServe llmisvc-controller\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDelivers standalone KEDA as a first-class autoscaling path for LLMInferenceService in the\n41\tKServe llmisvc-controller, alongside the existing WVA-mediated path, following the upstream\n42\tdesign kserve/kserve#5646 and its implementation PR kserve/kserve#5839. Users configure\n43\tKEDA triggers directly in the LLMInferenceService spec without deploying WVA, bringing\n44\tparity with v1beta1 InferenceService. The change is delivered either by consuming the\n45\tmerged upstream PR or by carrying the patch downstream (per the strategy's risk\n46\tmitigation), including any OpenShift-specific adaptation identified by the upstream\n47\tadaptation investigation.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- API type changes in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_types.go`: a\n52\t  standalone KEDA spec at the ScalingSpec level with `pollingInterval`, `cooldownPeriod`,\n53\t  and a `triggers` field for user-defined KEDA trigger definitions (type, metadata map).\n54\t- CEL validation changes in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_validation.go`:\n55\t  relax the requirement from `has(self.wva)` to at-least-one-of `wva` or `keda`, with\n56\t  mutual exclusivity enforced and trigger completeness validated; for disaggregated\n57\t  deployments, both prefill and decode phases must use the same scaling path (actuator\n58\t  consistency, overlay 0011).\n59\t- Controller changes in `pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/scaling.go`: branch on the\n60\t  configured path — standalone KEDA creates a ScaledObject from user-provided triggers and\n61\t  skips VariantAutoscaling CR creation entirely. The v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA\n62\t  reconciler at `pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/reconcilers/keda/keda_reconciler.go`\n63\t  is the reference implementation for trigger construction (Resource, External, PodMetric\n64\t  trigger types).\n65\t- Scaling status conditions and events for the standalone path (signal attribution for\n66\t  operators).\n67\t- Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0`; disaggregated deployments support\n68\t  independent per-phase scaling via phase-specific ScaledObjects.\n69\t- Integration testing across standalone KEDA with both deployment topologies (monolithic\n70\t  and disaggregated), including validation of the assumptions that KEDA\n71\t  `idleReplicaCount: 0` correctly pauses and resumes scaling for LLM inference workloads,\n72\t  and that EPP flow control queue metrics remain available when pods are at zero replicas.\n73\t- Backwards compatibility: static deployments with no `spec.scaling` and existing\n74\t  `spec.scaling.wva` deployments continue to work identically (additive change).\n75\t\n76\tOut of scope: standalone HPA without WVA (identified upstream as a potential follow-up),\n77\tauto-installation of KEDA (platform policy overlay 0008), multi-cluster autoscaling, and\n78\tcold-start time reduction (separate RFEs).\n79\t\n80\t## Acceptance Criteria\n81\t\n82\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` configured with user-defined\n83\t  triggers and no WVA deployed, when the trigger condition is met (e.g., Prometheus query\n84\t  threshold exceeded), then the deployment scales up, measured by KEDA ScaledObject status\n85\t  showing active and Deployment replica count increasing.\n86\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with both `spec.scaling.wva` and `spec.scaling.keda` set,\n87\t  when the CR is submitted, then the API server rejects it with a CEL validation error\n88\t  indicating mutual exclusivity.\n89\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` and no `spec.scaling.wva`, when\n90\t  the llmisvc-controller reconciles, then no VariantAutoscaling CR is created and a\n91\t  ScaledObject with the user-provided triggers is created, measured by\n92\t  `kubectl get variantautoscalings` returning empty and `kubectl get scaledobjects`\n93\t  returning a ScaledObject with the user's triggers.\n94\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with KEDA and `idleReplicaCount: 0` (either path), when no\n95\t  requests are received for the cooldown period, then the deployment scales to zero,\n96\t  measured by Deployment replica count reaching 0 and KEDA ScaledObject status showing idle.\n97\t- Given a disaggregated LLMInferenceService with separate scaling configs (either path),\n98\t  when prefill pods reach saturation while decode pods remain below threshold, then only\n99\t  the prefill pool scales up, measured by independent scaling resource status for prefill\n100\t  and decode roles.\n101\t- Given a deployment with autoscaling active (either path), when Prometheus metrics become\n102\t  unavailable, then the deployment holds its current replica count, measured by replica\n103\t  count remaining stable during the metric outage. (Flagged in the decomposition as\n104\t  dependent on KEDA operator behavior — verify feasibility against KEDA's error handling\n105\t  for metric source outages.)\n106\t- Static deployments with no autoscaling configured continue to serve identically,\n107\t  measured by no VariantAutoscaling, HPA, or ScaledObject resources created for\n108\t  deployments without `spec.scaling`.\n109\t- Scaling events are visible to operators for the standalone path, measured by KEDA\n110\t  ScaledObject events and scaling status conditions on the LLMInferenceService reporting\n111\t  the active path and attribution.\n112\t- The standalone KEDA support is consumable in the RHOAI-downstream llmisvc-controller,\n113\t  either via the merged upstream kserve/kserve#5839 or via a downstream carry of the\n114\t  patch (with backport once merged) — the fallback documented in the strategy's risk\n115\t  mitigation — whichever the upstream adaptation investigation recommends.\n116\t- The per-namespace TriggerAuthentication resources provisioned for LLMInferenceService\n117\t  standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers on OpenShift are available for user trigger\n118\t  definitions to reference (provisioned by the odh-model-controller work stream; a\n119\t  configuration reference, not a build dependency).\n120\t\n121\t## HLR Traceability\n122\t\n123\t- HLR-1 (P0): standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without WVA.\n124\t- HLR-2 (P0): mutual exclusivity of the two autoscaling paths via CEL validation.\n125\t- HLR-3 (P0): scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0`.\n126\t- HLR-4 (P0): scale-from-zero via user-configured triggers (mechanism; recommended\n127\t  trigger configurations are documented in the documentation work stream).\n128\t- HLR-5 (P0): disaggregated prefill/decode independent scaling.\n129\t- HLR-6 (P1): scaling events visible to operators with signal attribution (standalone\n130\t  path; bundled here because status conditions share the same API surface and\n131\t  reconciliation path as the P0 work).\n132\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-932df1256081f5ad","agent_id":"a23ebb4bbaff35dfc","session_id":"c67b7b09-8e50-4c38-b7b7-230c45313c19","uuid":"8f6161ef-e429-4baa-9957-2c1e27e1fe8a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:43:56.891Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a497dee97a469bfb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
