{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9344df8b05f584fa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: epic-decompose\n3\tdescription: Decompose batches of RHAISTRAT strategies into implementation epic DAGs. Accepts explicit IDs or a JQL query. Non-interactive.\n4\tuser-invocable: true\n5\tallowed-tools: Glob, Bash, Agent\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\tYou are a non-interactive epic decomposition pipeline. Do not ask questions or wait for confirmation. Make all decisions autonomously.\n9\t\n10\t## Turn Discipline (critical)\n11\t\n12\tYou run headless. **A response that contains only text and no tool call ends the session and aborts the pipeline mid-run.** Until the dispatch loop returns `done`, every one of your turns MUST end with a tool call — never with prose.\n13\t\n14\tIn particular, after you launch a wave's Agent(s), do **not** write narration such as \"the agent is running, waiting for it to complete.\" That text-only turn terminates the pipeline before the wave is collected. Your very next action, in the **same turn** as (or immediately after) the launch, MUST be the `wait-for-wave` Bash call. Do not describe what you are about to do — do it. Save any commentary for after the pipeline reaches `DONE`.\n15\t\n16\t## Setup\n17\t\n18\tParse `$ARGUMENTS` for:\n19\t- `--jql \"<query>\"`, `--limit N`, `--batch-size N` (default 25), `--data-dir \"<path>\"`\n20\t- `--headless`, `--announce-complete`, `--reprocess`, `--skip-if-has-epics`\n21\t- Remaining arguments: explicit RHAISTRAT IDs\n22\t\n23\t### 1. Init\n24\t\n25\t```bash\n26\tpython3 scripts/pipeline_state.py init [--batch-size N] [--headless] [--announce-complete]\n27\t```\n28\t\n29\t### 2. IDs\n30\t\n31\t**JQL mode** (`--jql`):\n32\t\n33\t```bash\n34\tpython3 scripts/fetch_strategy.py fetch \"<query>\" --ids-file tmp/pipeline-all-ids.txt [--limit N] [--data-dir \"<path>\"] [--skip-if-has-epics]\n35\t```\n36\t\n37\tPrint `[DECOMPOSE] JQL: <jql>` from stderr output.\n38\t\n39\t**Explicit mode**:\n40\t\n41\t```bash\n42\tpython3 scripts/state.py write-ids tmp/pipeline-all-ids.txt <IDs>\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\tIf no IDs and no JQL, stop with usage instructions.\n46\t\n47\t### 3. Bootstrap\n48\t\n49\t```bash\n50\tbash scripts/fetch-architecture-context.sh\n51\tpython3 scripts/fetch_components.py\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tRetry each once on failure. If retry fails, stop: \"bootstrap failed.\"\n55\t\n56\t### 4. Resume check + batch\n57\t\n58\tRead all IDs: `python3 scripts/state.py read-ids tmp/pipeline-all-ids.txt`\n59\t\n60\tSplit into batches of `batch_size`. Write each:\n61\t\n62\t```bash\n63\tpython3 scripts/state.py write-ids tmp/pipeline-batch-1-ids.txt <batch_1_IDs>\n64\tpython3 scripts/state.py write-ids tmp/pipeline-batch-2-ids.txt <batch_2_IDs>\n65\t```\n66\t\n67\tStart the pipeline:\n68\t\n69\t```bash\n70\tpython3 scripts/pipeline_state.py set total_batches=<M>\n71\tpython3 scripts/pipeline_state.py set-phase BATCH_START\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\t## Dispatch Loop\n75\t\n76\tRepeat until action is `done`:\n77\t\n78\t### Step 1: Get next action\n79\t\n80\t```bash\n81\tpython3 scripts/pipeline_state.py next-action\n82\t```\n83\t\n84\tParse the YAML output for: `action`, `phase`, `message`, `agents`.\n85\t\n86\t### Step 2: Execute\n87\t\n88\t**done**: Exit loop. Run teardown.\n89\t\n90\t**run_script**: Run `python3 scripts/pipeline_state.py run-phase`. Go to step 1.\n91\t\n92\t**launch_wave**: For each agent in the `agents` list:\n93\t- Build prompt: `\"<vars>\\n\\nRead <prompt_file> and follow all instructions exactly.\"`\n94\t- `vars` are pre-rendered KEY=VALUE lines with `{ID}` already substituted.\n95\t- Launch as background Agent (with `subagent_type` if present).\n96\t\n97\tImmediately wait for completion. **Do not end your turn or emit any text after launching — your next tool call MUST be `wait-for-wave`:**\n98\t\n99\t```bash\n100\tpython3 scripts/pipeline_state.py wait-for-wave\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tOn exit 0 (complete): go to step 1.\n104\tOn exit 3 (still pending): re-run `python3 scripts/pipeline_state.py wait-for-wave` as your next tool call — do not write any text between attempts, as a text-only turn would terminate the pipeline.\n105\tAny other exit code is an error.\n106\t\n107\t### Example `launch_wave` output\n108\t\n109\t```yaml\n110\taction: launch_wave\n111\tphase: DECOMPOSE\n112\tmessage: \"DECOMPOSE: wave 1/2 (5 IDs)\"\n113\tagents:\n114\t  - prompt_file: skills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md\n115\t    vars: |\n116\t      ID=RHAISTRAT-1234\n117\t```\n118\t\n119\t## Teardown\n120\t\n121\tAfter phase reaches `DONE`:\n122\t\n123\t```bash\n124\tpython3 scripts/batch_summary.py --counts-only $(python3 scripts/state.py read-ids tmp/pipeline-all-ids.txt)\n125\t```\n126\t\n127\t$ARGUMENTS\n128\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-932df1256081f5ad","agent_id":"a23ebb4bbaff35dfc","session_id":"c67b7b09-8e50-4c38-b7b7-230c45313c19","uuid":"2099f79c-b6a5-4a87-a544-b870827f9784","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:46:19.327Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9344df8b05f584fa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
