{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-5382c12a-6b01-4a6b-85bf-987734bbedb3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9018c2257b693ba6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-fmmxljnz/artifacts/epic-reviews/RHAISTRAT-8008-decomp-review.md","content":"## Review Summary\n\nScore: 13/14 — pass\nRecommendation: accept\n\nFull decomposition of an M-effort, multi-component strategy into 4 epics (1\nInvestigation, 3 Implementation including one docs-authoring). Triage is null, so\nmulti-epic output is expected; epic_count (4) matches the epic list. The DAG is\nacyclic, diagram and frontmatter dependencies agree exactly, and every edge is\njustified by a construction rule. The only deduction is a sizing concern on E002.\n\n## Criterion Details\n\n### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\nAll 7 HLRs map to at least one epic (HLR-1/2/3/4/5 → E002, HLR-1 → E003 for the\nOpenShift Prometheus trigger source, HLR-4/7 → E004); the traceability matrix in\nthe decomposition summary is present and matches each epic's own HLR\nTraceability section. No P2 HLRs exist. Priority inheritance is correct: E001 is\nP0 because it blocks all P0 implementation work; E002/E003 are P0 (HLR-1..5);\nE004 is a `docs-authoring` epic exempt from priority inheritance and correctly\nderives P0 from the strategy's Critical priority. The HLR-6 (P1) bundle inside\nE002 is not priority collapse: scaling status conditions share the same\nScalingSpec API surface and controller reconciliation path as the P0 work, so\nunder the priority-split rule (independent value AND no shared API surface) the\nbundle is correct and the summary documents the justification.\n\n### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\nEdges: E001→E002, E001→E003, E002→E003, E002→E004, E003→E004. All five edges in\nthe mermaid diagram (drawn dependency → dependent, correct convention) have\nmatching `dependencies` entries in the target epics' front