e. The decomposition acknowledges this in Health\nWarnings with a documented split trigger (integration testing into its own epic\nif the estimate firms up at 2+ sprints) and a reasonable cohesion argument (one\nAPI surface, one reconciliation path; upstream #5839 as reference). Slightly\noversized, not clearly multi-sprint; one point deducted. Minor issue logged.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (downstream adaptation needs,\ncarry-vs-wait) changes what E002 and E003 must include, and both list it in\n`dependencies` with `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-8008-E001`. Both `gate_failure_impact`\nentries are fully populated with action (rewrite / add_remediation) and\nfallback_approach, and both are true gates — the outcome changes downstream\nscope, not merely scheduling. E002/E003 produce concrete code artifacts; E004\nproduces documentation. No epic lists an Investigation dependency without\n`gated_by`; both `gated_by` targets appear in the epic's direct `dependencies`.\nE004 correctly has no gate. No misclassifications.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nE001 uses `investigation_signals` (ai_signals null); E002/E003/E004 use\n`ai_signals` (investigation_signals null) — correct signal sets per type. All\nfour ai-signals rationale files exist and their tables match the frontmatter\nvalues exactly. Spot checks against the rubrics: E001\n`question_specificity: 1` (concrete, enumerable question with definable\npass/fail), `source_accessibility: 1` (the PR diff plus RHOAI-consumed sources\ndetermine the adaptation answer; only the peripheral merge-timeline is\nuncertain), `local_runnability: 0` (controllers cannot be exercised as plain\nlocal binaries — cluster required), `cluster_hardware_dependence: 0` (gating\nquestion is source-readable per the rubric's controller-generates note),\n`human_judgment_required: -1` (peripheral carry-vs-wait stakeholder call).\nE002's `open_questions/external_dependency/human_process_gates: -1` are\nconsistent with the unresolved upstream adaptation question and in-progress\nupstream PR; E003's `external_dependency: 0` is consistent (RHOAI-owned repo;\nthe kserve API-types dependency is modeled as an internal DAG edge, as the\nrationale explains); E004's `human_process_gates: -1` matches the mandatory\ndocs technical review. No rubric contradictions; arithmetic not checked per\ninstructions.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable given/when/then ACs derived from the strategy's seven\nacceptance criteria, with concrete measurements (kubectl checks, ScaledObject\nstatus, replica counts). Rule-mandated ACs: Rule 24 (docs technical review) is\npresent on E004 (\"passes the Red Hat docs content process including technical\nreview by the implementing engineering teams\"); Rule 23 (rollback/feature-flag)\nis not triggered — the change is additive, not a replacement — and E002 still\ncarries backwards-compatibility ACs for static and WVA deployments; Rule 25\n(build pipeline green) is N/A (no konflux-onboarding in any dependency chain).\nEpic bodies do not reference sibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic references\nuse work-stream descriptions (\"the odh-model-controller work stream\"), which is\ncorrect for Jira. The metric-outage AC feasibility concern is honestly flagged\nin both the summary and the E002 AC itself.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nAll strategy scope is accounted for: API/validation/controller changes and both\ndeployment topologies (E002), TriggerAuthentication auth context with lifecycle\ncleanup and TLS 1.2+ (E003), and the full documentation surface — decision\nguide, per-shape recipes, scale-to/from-zero guidance with EPP-queue trigger\ntemplates, cold-start expectations, KEDA prerequisite install guidance,\nTriggerAuthentication operator instructions, fleet-scale Prometheus capacity\nguidance, troubleshooting, supported configuration matrix (E004). All seven\nstrategy acceptance criteria appear as epic ACs. Strategy-level context is\ncarried forward, not dropped: the upstream-delay risk (patch-carry fallback AC\non E002 plus the E001 investigation), scale-from-zero reliability and cold-start\nrisks (E004 scope), KEDA non-auto-install policy (E004), the scalability NFR\nwith no measurable target (flagged as a health warning with E004 capacity\nguidance), and all three open questions (E001 gate; p50/p95 and capacity\nguidance as E004 ACs). NFRs: backwards compatibility and security have explicit\nACs; observability maps to HLR-6. Out-of-scope items (standalone HPA, KEDA\nauto-install, multi-cluster, cold-start reduction) are correctly excluded. A\ndocs-authoring epic exists even though the strategy's Documentation Support gate\nonly reads \"Pending human review\" — the correct outcome given HLR-7. No\nconditional branches are used, and none are needed: the upstream-PR uncertainty\nis handled via gate metadata and tiered delivery, which covers all outcomes.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45625,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-932df1256081f5ad","agent_id":"a23ebb4bbaff35dfc","session_id":"c67b7b09-8e50-4c38-b7b7-230c45313c19","uuid":"04536699-8ab2-4323-864e-327a9b485546","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:48:55.275Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
